nodecode-api-indonesia is a rewrite of khmuhtadin's khmuhtadin/api-indonesia-examples:

  https://github.com/khmuhtadin/api-indonesia-examples
  commit 73d9d4bc060ad4814d0c95c9b3f5f328d07858d5
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Khaisa Studio (Khairul Muhtadin) (LICENSE)

Rewritten: what the package is -- a front end to API Indonesia's hosted MCP
server at https://mcp.apiindonesia.id/mcp, reached with an aip_live_ key, and
holding Indonesian public data from official sources (regions down to
villages, postal codes, holidays, prayer times, BMKG, schools, hospitals,
exchange rates, minimum wage, halal, BPOM, OJK, KBBI, Al-Quran and more).
The manifests' facts became the cell's section (the endpoint, the REST base,
the key's environment variable, the timeout) and the verbs the server's own
tool set needs: one that lists it and one that calls into it, both speaking
the server's protocol (MCP over Streamable HTTP) with the core's own HTTP
seam. The bundled skill -- its endpoint table, the warning that a NIK or NPWP
check is a format check, that the source in the answer's metadata is cited,
and what a 401 and a 402 mean -- is the manual topic and the tool
descriptions. The examples' REST style (the x-api-key header, the same host)
became a third verb, api_indonesia_get, so a documented path is still
reachable when the tool set served at run time lacks what a task needs.

Left out, and why: the example clients in curl, JavaScript, PHP, Python and
n8n, and the configs for other clients (mcp.json, .mcp.json, server.json,
.claude-plugin/plugin.json) all show how to reach the same two endpoints from
somewhere else, and a cell needs one; the Python requirements file exists to
run one of them. None of it runs here, and no Node, python, pip or npx
mcp-remote bridge is needed. The server's ~30 products' tool descriptions
are not copied, since the server serves them at run time and a copy would go
stale; the skill's endpoint table is kept because it is the fallback's map.
